# Line endings.
#
# Everything this repo tracks is either source or a data file with a defined
# format, and the pipeline writes LF on every platform (see the NEWLINE constant
# in synthetic_data/focusbridge/core/jsonio.py).
#
# Without the rule below, a clone on Windows checks these files out as CRLF -
# and the very next pipeline run rewrites all 200 of them back to LF, producing
# 200 "modified" files with no content change whatsoever. Pinning eol=lf makes
# the working tree agree with what the code writes, so `git status` only ever
# reports things that actually changed.
#
# `text=auto` still auto-detects binaries, so the app icons are left alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# students.jsonl is 160 MB, over GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit, so it is stored
# with Git LFS. `-text` disables all newline conversion for it, and this line
# must come AFTER the wildcard above in order to win.
students.jsonl filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
